insert into _dr_upd (id, code, n, upd) values
('p11','EAS-2025-CCR-005',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"1) Stella approved best performance setup\n2) Awaiting finalization by purchasing next week\n3) Contract signature planned for Nov and GoLive for new providers for 1st of Feb 2027\n4) Supplier are not informed yet! As there might be another round of price negotiations. Changing markets where informed (FR; IT, PL, CZ & SLO, FI & Baltics)","by":"黄浩 Cokey"}$j$::jsonb),
('p18','EAS-2026-TRN-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"Training Centre Planner developed (Business Plan, Centre Grade, Tools & Equipment, Running Cost)\nTools & equipment list and budget by centre grade (A–D) completed\nTraining demand for new service shops 2026–2030 in progress","by":"黄浩 Cokey"}$j$::jsonb),
('p19','EAS-2026-TRN-002',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"- Account management – [completed / in final testing and adding the users this week], user roles and permissions set up (admin, trainer, ...), account creation and deactivation flow, password reset / login]\n\n- Digital Tools & Database separation – bugs fixed, performance improvements]\n\n- AI Assistance – [started / concept defined]\n[e.g. use cases defined (FAQ, course search, user guidance), first prototype, chosen platform]\nNext steps:  AI switch to BYD provided AI","by":"黄浩 Cokey"}$j$::jsonb),
('p30','EAS-2025-UKR-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"I submitted a closure project on this last month. The firsy performance report and KPIs are being produced any day now. The programme has seen the most instructions from all other programmes which was communicated and some of the KPIs look promising on inspection. When all the insurers KPIs are submitted we will get a national overview of the key KPIs, it will be an indepth report which will offer a clear performance of the programme.","by":"Maurizio Pisano"}$j$::jsonb),
('p30','EAS-2025-UKR-001',1,$j${"date":"2026-10-07","text":"UK Bodyshop are active and operational 137. We have now added a link on the website showing all the BYD Bodyshops and BYD retailers supplying parts nationwide swo we have full transparentcy. Parts supply has been good, we havnt experienced any issues around availability to date, this is monitored daily. End of October we will have our first UK reporting on the programme covering all key KPIs. Auto Asia continue to cause issues around parts blaming BYD when its not BYD, I have already spoken to the majority of insurance companies who have agreed to use BYD retailers going forward for parts. Bodyshop network now has consistant discounts for insurers at 15% and labour rates have been sustained between £30-£40 an hour keeping repairs costs fully under control and giving the iinsurers much needed stability on pricing.","by":"Maurizio Pisano"}$j$::jsonb),
('p31','EAS-2025-UKR-002',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"UK team, Benny, Liam viewed over 10 locations and all of them didnt meet expectations. Benny has instructed a Manchester agent to locate further locations in Manchester to view, we are waiting for the recommendations to view. Manchester is the location that is being selected as this is Stellas preferred location. We did find an excllent location at Mira industrial park with race track and facilities but it was outside Birmingham but it was declined as Manchester has to be location. We continue to source the right location agreed by the UK team.","by":"Maurizio Pisano"}$j$::jsonb),
('p39','EAS-2026-UKR-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"For UK, we have done some work in the back. we have reached out to our approved body shop and we can do 8 battery repair centres with them. will be signed off shortly we have done all the communications with them already. plus we will be selective for our retailers, 2 in Scottland are agreed, but haven't signed yet. still looking for one in Manchester city, one in Birmingham, one in West midlands, 2 in London and 1 in Wales. \n\nwe have order 10 sets of mandatory tools for the battery repairs from China, back order but will be here shortly. just had the newest price file for special tools, it will cost 7,000 Euro. \n\nalso, Malta and Cyprus will be signed off as well. We haven't included Ireland because they are in the transition from D+ to NSC.","by":"Maurizio Pisano"}$j$::jsonb),
('p46','EAS-2026-DE-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"Monthly Invoicing:\n1. #45781 Complete Note, RRP, discount, logistics dates and total quantity in the Delivery Note list and Excel export\nhttps://as.coding.byd.com/p/OverseasBSS/requirements/issues/45781/detail （not yet started）\n\n2. #48818 Add PDF download and printing to the Delivery Note details page\nhttps://as.coding.byd.com/p/OverseasBSS/requirements/issues/48818/detail （not yet started）\n\n3. Finance: SAP functionality not yet imeplemented succefully. Follow up with Finance today\n\nSEPA:\n1. Sideletter signing: 127/175\n2. Sideletter as part of SA: 26/26\n3. BNP mandates collected: 122/201\n\nCHALLENGES :\n\nIssues with BNP Portal – various blockers\nEnormous delay in portal availability from BNP\nDelayed Access to portal - for BYD team\nHad to creae BYD specific landing page for expired links \nTest system picked up various bugs in system which needed to be solved by BNP\nTedious and long process to gather and assign dealers eligible to receive the mandate (i.e signed SA/sideletter) \nSome bugs fixed but live system still contains bugs – e.g Links expiring before 48 hours! Which means Links need to be resent. \nAdditional issues for Finance team to create the transactions\n\nManual Follow Up Process\nCompilation of list of dealers to send mandates to needs to be aligned to O&C status list of signed agreements, we need to await updates and need constant follow up with O&C\nNeeded to manually create individual reference mandate numbers for quick identification by dealer and location\nProactive guidelines and email notifications were sent to dealers just before they received the mandate link\nPositive : batch upload possible, however due to various bugs in the system, we elected to send between 20-50 at a time – to mange efficiently. \nLink resend process is manual and individual\nLink to mandate only valid 48 hours and once opened, dealer has just 30 minutes to complete the E-signature!\nList of contacts identified as authourized to sign – some left the company or out of office – causing additional delays\nTime consuming Individual follow up‘s with dealers - to support them in the signature process\n\n=> regardless of all of the above we are ready to start SEPA prior to monthly invoicing, but BNP must aggregate invoice amounts on weekly basis and must display invoice number data....confirmation from BNP pending\n\nSBI:\n1. Sideletter signed: 127/175\n2. Sideletter as part of SA: 26/26\n3. Bankdata inserted in BSS: 70/201\n\n#48710 Add the third-party system work-order number to the claim-settlement list and PDF/Excel exports\nhttps://as.coding.byd.com/p/OverseasBSS/requirements/issues/48710/detail （half done）\n\n#48629 Payment-flow creation failure for the 169W claim settlement (uploadFileInfo fail)\nhttps://as.coding.byd.com/p/OverseasBSS/bug-tracking/issues/48629 (in process)\n\n=> awaiting feedback from IT team today on progress\n\nChallenges: Dealer Council intervened about notice period prior to SEPA debit...7 days agreed with FInance but 3 days stated in contract...talkls ongoing to remove this block","by":"Daglef Seeck"}$j$::jsonb),
('p47','EAS-2026-DE-002',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"1. Building Alteration Application\n=> All documents approved, PoA approved but not signed yet by Stella.\n=> correction of previous updates (misunderstanding internally)\n=> No reaction by Lexi since 8 weeks\n=> Now we kick off another OA process to gain signature\n=> Procurement changed instruction despite all prior approvals in order to allow the architect to acutally insert the application in the city system\n=> another OA process required and escalation meeting taking place today in parallel (3/11 9 am)\n\n2. Landlord does not receive any rent so far and the risk to loose the entire object is increasing\n\n=> update 4/11: PoA topic resolved. Architect will become \"general contractor\" and is thus empowered to perform the admin process in the city portal\n=> Signature of Stella is no longer required","by":"Daglef Seeck"}$j$::jsonb),
('p48','EAS-2026-DE-003',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"1. ALSA feedback provided\n2. According to SA 2.2 all service shops are required to be able to  perform repairs on HV vehicles\n3. no additional contract necessary\n4. Only training and special tools need to be prepared and secured followed by partners needing to be enabled for L1\n5. no special authorization process required\n6. L2 and L3 follow the same tracks\n7. we contacted several partners already to invite for training","by":"Daglef Seeck"}$j$::jsonb),
('p58','EAS-2026-BNB-004',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"GDPR clause cleared and product offering went live on Fragus sales portal 2nd of November. Official dealer communication planned this week.","by":"Marius Revhaug"}$j$::jsonb),
('p59','EAS-2026-BNB-005',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"Contract details under development, final review from business side (market) this week. \nNew partners onboarding started. Technical training next week in Gothenburg (cw 46).","by":"Peter Andersson"}$j$::jsonb),
('p60','EAS-2026-BNB-006',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"Local training solution canceled, leading to new meetings to offer the centralized training. \nDealer 1 (LECAB) have problems following our suggested timeline, but will join once approved by the owners.\nDealer 2 (Bendt bil) will join most likely, but their new HV expert (former Porsche) joins the company in january 2027.  Other dealers have no capacity for HV batteyr at this point.","by":"Peter Andersson"}$j$::jsonb),
('p61','EAS-2026-BNB-007',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"1. Confirm  with 12 dealership with  power battery  repare capabilty for other OME In NL. and in the porgess introduce BYD the power battery service standand and request.\n\n2. Currently working with the aftersales team of the  Division 2 to identify potential third-party battery repair centers. one potential partner (Autocradft Solution Group)  in progress discussions the further cooperation.","by":"黄明辉Brent"}$j$::jsonb),
('p64','EAS-2026-FRA-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"Updated layout and design enhancements shared with internal stakeholders.\nQuotations received from lift suppliers; awaiting landlord’s final approval to install two lifts.\nBNP continues to support lighting adjustments and facility improvements, including the BYD Service logo on the back wall.","by":"王睿Clara  Wang"}$j$::jsonb),
('p70','EAS-2026-FRA-004',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"ICARE and the new financing partner have defined the service contract offers.\nNext step: Roll out service packages bundled with financing in France, once the CGI agreement is finalized.\nInternal discussions ongoing with EU Aftersales to define BYD standalone service packages.","by":"王睿Clara  Wang"}$j$::jsonb),
('p73','EAS-2026-FRA-006',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"Service provider identified: Autoeco.\nScope: waste collection traceability across the BYD aftersales network, environmental regulatory monitoring and compliance reporting.\nCommercial offer and contract shared with Legal for review.\nNext step: Contract validation","by":"王睿Clara  Wang"}$j$::jsonb),
('p74','EAS-2026-FRA-007',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"First step: All BYD dealers requested to confirm their existing HV battery repair capabilities.\nDefined a four-step network development plan:\nIdentify qualified repair sites.\nAssess technical capabilities, equipment and safety standards.\nProvide BYD training, certification and authorization.\nLaunch one pilot center and evaluate performance before expansion.","by":"王睿Clara  Wang"}$j$::jsonb),
('p75','EAS-2025-ITA-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"2110 Operational meeting with Bosch and SAOL to define the operating workflows, warranty claim process, and VDS invoicing process. The model will follow an L1 (SAOL) and L2 (BCS) support structure. The three-party agreement is in reviewing by legal teams. Next steps: share the proposal with the commercial team (Blair) for alignment and contract signature. In parallel, finalize the agreement between BYD Italy and Bosch covering network development activities and BCS activation costs.","by":"Enea Costa"}$j$::jsonb),
('p80','EAS-2025-ITA-002',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"0910 The facility has been identified. The design consultancy is currently preparing a cost estimate for reinforcing the floor slabs to support the installation of workshop lifts. In parallel, the Procurement team is finalizing and negotiating the lease agreement.","by":"Enea Costa"}$j$::jsonb),
('p88','EAS-2026-ITA-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"Service Point rollout with Approved Body Shops is ongoing. The first service appointed: Lozza Milan, Veloccia Rome, and Naples (meeting with investor scheduled for 11 of november). In parallel, we are awaiting a quotation from Lozza for the development of the Approved Body Shop portal in cooperation with Solera.","by":"Enea Costa"}$j$::jsonb),
('p91','EAS-2026-ITA-004',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"HV Battery Repair Workshop Implementation Strategy: \n- Ready for publication of the circular with tools list and minimum requirements. \n- Awaiting feedback from HQ to avoid the need for contract amendments.\nOnce HQ guidance is received, the dealer selection and activation plan will be finalized.","by":"Enea Costa"}$j$::jsonb),
('p106','EAS-2025-IBR-006',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"+ Bi-weekly meeting with Bolttech\n+ Working on Leads dashboard\n+ Next steps: New Dealers to be included\n+ New hiring - In progress\n+ Meeting with ERSM: Responsabilities definition - Agreement","by":"Jesús Javier Pérez Blanco"}$j$::jsonb),
('p117','EAS-2026-IBR-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"+ Project finished from Aftersales team on time.\n+ Financing dept. is managing the legal text to be included in Dealers invoicing because now all the payments will be submitted every day 15th of the month.","by":"Jesús Javier Pérez Blanco"}$j$::jsonb),
('p118','EAS-2026-IBR-002',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"+ Strategy: Certificate to all Dealers which accomplish the BYD requeriments\n+ Waiting for feedback by HQ regarding to the new contract / Anex to be signed by Dealers\n+ Gathering information about current Dealers certification in L1 / L2 / L3 battery reparation to figure out the requeriments set by Spanish regulation \n            - Dealer responsabilities, mandatory roles in Dealers \n            - technicians + expert in fire extinghised,  \n            - battery storage, \n            - goberment authorities - firefighters procedures..\n+ Meeting with Dealers: Caetano, Quadis, Icamotor, Pyreness\n            - Wednesday, November 4th\n            - Thursday, November 5th","by":"Jesús Javier Pérez Blanco"}$j$::jsonb),
('p120','EAS-2025-CEE-004',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"4. Training will take place during the first week of December.","by":"黄明辉 Brent"}$j$::jsonb),
('p133','EAS-2025-CEE-012',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"2. Both will submit a workshop project plan and an implementation timeline.","by":"黄明辉 Brent"}$j$::jsonb),
('p134','EAS-2025-CEE-013',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"3. Following the signing of the contract, they will order the special tools\nfrom BYD.","by":"黄明辉 Brent"}$j$::jsonb),
('p136','EAS-2026-CEE-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"Project presentation for the new Head of Fleet – done\nFleet contract for clients – in progress\nFleet programme for service shops – in progress, CFM conditions announced\nStrategy change following discussions with BYD’s finance department; transfer of the fleet module to BSS – i.e. the customer identification module, the repair/servicing authorisation module (based on warranty claims process) and the central billing module – discussions with BYD’s IT department","by":"Mariusz Kiljańczyk"}$j$::jsonb),
('p137','EAS-2026-CEE-002',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"1.  Candidates have provided feedback on the contract.\n2. Candidates will submit a workshop project plan and an implementation timeline.\n3. Following the signing of the contract, they will order the special tools from BYD.\n4. Training will take place during the first week of December.","by":"Marek Raninec"}$j$::jsonb),
('p144','EAS-2026-SEE-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"1) contract agreed by both party. signing process pending by Stella.\n2) the technician attending the training had been confirmed. waiting for training arrangement releasing.\n3) all tool&equipment purchased. checking the arriving status","by":"张绩 Jay"}$j$::jsonb),
('p154','EAS-2026-CAC-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"Overall project progress: 70%\n1. Internationalized terms for the transparent workshop system have been finalized; translation into Uzbek language is in progress.\n2. The PIA for overseas Open workshop data compliance has been submitted, and resources for overseas production servers have been requested.\n3. Developers are expected to arrive at the Tashkent dealershop by the end of November to conduct equipment and functionality testing.\n4. The hardware procurement list has been informed to dealers.\n5. BSS Integration: Joint debugging of BSS-related interfaces is 60% complete; store information and store staff details are being finalized.","by":"陈彦Charlie"}$j$::jsonb),
('p155','EAS-2026-CAC-002',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"1. Reviewed the legal aspects of new training center premises and rental cost；\n2.Regular Training holding in Sergelie training center","by":"陈彦Charlie"}$j$::jsonb),
('p157','EAS-2026-CAC-003',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"1. Supplier quotes have been finalized.\n2. The mystery shopper inspection standards for Central Asia after-sales service have been issued.\n3. A meeting with suppliers is planned to conduct a pilot mystery shopper visit at one store.","by":"陈彦Charlie"}$j$::jsonb),
('p159','EAS-2026-CAC-023',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-04","text":"1. Contract is not signed yet. Distrubitor' Legal Department is reviewing. Target for completion is 16 Nov.\n2. 45 vehicles repaired so far. 17 more vehicles have technical approved. Monthly failures is about 15.\n3. 32 technician completed and passed the training. After last training on 13 Nov, all dealers will have qualified technicians. Total techs will be 55.\n4. No special SST needed for fusebox replacement. Dealers use their existing isolation tools.\nSST is needed for the next level (pack opening and replacement).\nSST order is placed. No ETA yet.\nPart orders are planned to cover the next 5 months.\n5. We request training for next-level pack repairs.\n6. We are checking regulations on reusing old pre-charge failure batteries after fusebox replacement.\nWe have 10 such batteries.\nIf legally possible, we will complete the replacements quickly and make them ready for use.","by":"陈彦Charlie"}$j$::jsonb),
('p161','EAS-2025-PBS-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-11","text":"一、项目端-售后团队\n------------------------------\n\n——系统\n1、系统优化：AI自动审核功能已开发完毕，11月24号上线\n2、系统对接：\n（1）权益下发：已确认系统对接方案，正在推进中，预计1月30日上线，实现系统权益自动下发\n（2）销售对接：协助BGPC对接后续销售平台，待确认终版流程图\n（3）UCS在线支付方案：正在进行开发需求评估\n\n——项目保障\n1、权益维护：已明确权益内容，系统完成对接前手动维护，完成后系统自动化对接\n2、能力培训：各市场已完成认证培训或少量认证试点，具备及时开展认证能力\n\n\n二、市场端-大客户团队\n------------------------------\n\n1、经销商合同和激励政策：大客户预计11月20日同步timeline\n（1）待刷新合同模板，以及推进后续经销商签订\n（2）激励政策待大客户输出\n\n2、CPO KPI：11月初大客户与各国团队进行会议沟通，关于CPO的KPI标准，大客户仍在内部对齐中\n\n\n三、各市场进度及认证数据\n------------------------------\n\n——整体进度\n1、波兰经销商已开始认证并销售；西班牙堆场进行部分认证\n2、意大利、法国、英国规划11月底，荷兰12月底预计开始运营\n3、德国及其他国家计划待定\n\n——各市场：合计认证2882台","by":"黄浩 Cokey"}$j$::jsonb),
('p161','EAS-2025-PBS-001',1,$j${"date":"2026-10-28","text":"——系统\n1、系统优化：AI自动审核功能已开发完毕，待核验上线\n2、系统对接：\n（1）权益下发：已确认系统对接方案，正在推进中，预计1月30日上线，实现系统权益自动下发\n（2）销售对接：协助BGPC对接后续销售平台，待确认终版流程图\n（3）UCS在线支付方案：待各市场确认权益费用后拉通\n——项目保障\n1、权益维护：已明确权益内容，系统完成对接前手动维护，完成后系统自动化对接\n2、能力培训：各市场已完成认证培训或少量认证试点，具备及时开展认证能力\n\n市场端-大客户团队\n1、经销商合同：待刷新合同模板，以及推进后续经销商签订\n2、权益收费：待大客户同步方案宣导进度\n3、费用支付方式及激励政策：待大客户输出\n\n1、波兰：\n（1）经销商已开始认证\n（2）经销商账号28个，累计认证250台\n\n2、西班牙：\n（1）回购车已开始认证，经销商端正在与经销商协同推进\n（2）经销商账号21个，累计认证501台\n3. 法国：\n（1）10月开展全面培训，待首批回购车到港后全面正式运营，预计11月底开始认证\n4. 荷兰：\n（1）已完成堆场与经销商测试，预计堆场12月底开始运营\n（2）经销商账号11个","by":"黄浩 Cokey"}$j$::jsonb),
('p162','EAS-2025-PBS-002',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-11","text":"腾势精选好礼、惊喜交付和OTA升级方案已有，当前暂无变动；其他更新如下：\n\n泛欧道路救援： \n1. 供应商招标：正在问采购11.09向渤总汇报的情况\n2. APP在线救援：暂无更新\n3. 话务：暂无更新\n\n兆瓦闪充：\n1. 功能开发：暂无更新\n2. 闪充网络：\n1）现有桩安装情况：目前共建13套，奥地利新增1；5套桩上电\n2）仓库已到桩：计划4季度所有仓库的已到桩（30套）全部安装完毕\n\n维保取送车：App UI方案已评审，其他暂无新的进度\n\n代步车：暂无更新\n\n腾势游侠：\n1. 人员招聘（游侠/客关）：暂无更新\n2. 游侠培训：下一轮培训时间安排在27年Q1\n3. 服务车：DE确认使用店端二手车；NL/SE已开始准备车辆\n4. 车贴：暂无更新\n5. 工具箱：6套空运11.13前可以出关提货，下周各分公司可以收到；40套船运11.4已靠港，还在等待清关排期；已通知各分公司将收货信息发送给经销商，UK/DE/IT/NL/SE/CH已发送，其他市场暂未反馈；供应商可以提供线上订购平台，目前已搭建好，测试中，预计11.13前完成\n6. 备件：已与备件确认，根据备件计划，在国内有货的情况下，各国家仓十二月底配齐所需备件\n7. VDS：BSS APP开发进度待确认\n8. 制服：初始库存生产中；PR流程已结案；11.12和供应商讨论合同条款以及线上订购平台事宜\n9. 服务/维修三件套/脚垫：UK/ES/PL已有，UZ除维修三件套外已有；已确认维修三件套与供应商的合同过期，该物料已下架，中国和中亚都没有库存；荷兰仓有剩余库存138件，法国34件，英国25件，已通知区域可以从其他国家仓调货\n10. 系统功能：开发部分已基本完成，目前功能测试中","by":"黄浩 Cokey"}$j$::jsonb),
('p162','EAS-2025-PBS-002',1,$j${"date":"2026-10-28","text":"泛欧道路救援： \n1. 供应商招标：预算方案上周三已审批，目前等待会议纪要发布后进行二轮议价\n2. APP在线救援：API开发与号码展示排期0130，目前已完成一轮需求评审\n3. 话务：英、荷比卢已随APP930面客上线；法德意西、波兰、瑞士已随APP730面客上线\n\n远程专家：\n1. 功能已开放全市场门店技师权限，9月月活达到230+\n2. 流程方面：暂定功能呈现方式为在官网和App中展示有此功能，用户可按需联系经销商，目前正沟通开发计划\n\n兆瓦闪充：\n1. 功能开发：闪充APP预计11月底上线（视闪充桩开发情况），暂不考虑内嵌DENZA APP及积分兑换功能\n2. 闪充网络：\n1）现有桩安装情况：目前共建12套\n荷兰1 法国1 德国1 奥地利1 意大利1 保加利亚1\n乌兹4  哈萨克2\n2）仓库已到桩：\nUK4  瑞典4  挪威4  芬兰4  丹麦6\n西班牙3  葡萄牙2  意大利4  法国2\n德国2   奥地利1  荷兰2  克罗地亚3\n匈牙利：200+\n海外闪充团队正陆续下PO单— 找供应商安装\n（其他部署规划情况暂未公开）\n\n维保取送车：排期1230，APP功能方案评审中\n\n代步车：渠道进展待更新\n\n腾势游侠：\n1. 人员招聘：\n    A. 游侠：NL/SE各新增1名\n    B. 腾势客户关怀专员招聘：暂无更新\n2. 游侠培训：NL/SE新增游侠的培训时间预计安排在27年Q1（若新增游侠超过5名可安排提前培训）\n3. 服务车：暂无更新\n4. 车贴：暂无更新\n5. 工具箱：40套船运10.30靠港，6套空运上周已到，目前正在清关中；分公司都还在走预算审批流程，供应商确认可以先发货后付款，已向各分公司确认了收货信息，出来后立刻发出，预计11月上旬都能到位\n6. 备件：暂无更新\n7. VDS：功能已具备，BSS APP开发进度暂无更新\n8. 制服：已将所需尺码及数量（预计80套）发送给供应商，供应商准备库存中，计划十一月底准备完成；目前正在推进合同签署与PR流程\n9. 服务/维修三件套/脚垫：暂无更新\n10. 服务项目：计划本期（1130）仅上线诊断类功能，0130将按国家和车型上线服务项目，目前与市场沟通收集中\n11. 支付开票方案：支付方案已有，目前正与需上线市场一一确认发票合规","by":"黄浩 Cokey"}$j$::jsonb),
('p167','EAS-2026-PBS-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-11","text":"- BYD及DENZA App服务预约功能排期11月30日，试点与BSS及经销商DMS（Keyloop）的接口联调，打通三方预约接口及数据流。\n- 西班牙ODEC已完成三方预约平台开发，正接洽经销商DMS推进接口联调，后续计划复用现有三方预约接口方案。\n- DENZA官网预约模块计划11月24日开展UI评审，评审完成后推进开发；BYD官网待三方预约接口完成后安排开发排期","by":"黄浩 Cokey"}$j$::jsonb),
('p167','EAS-2026-PBS-001',1,$j${"date":"2026-10-28","text":"DENZA APP\n上周排查出联调bug, 本周解决，下周开放意大利，西班牙，波兰进行为期2周内测，完善客户链路。同步完善多市场运营规则。\n客户预约需求需经销商24小时确认，开放5天后预约时间。要求经销商预留一个腾势工位作为官方渠道预约，该工位分四个时段进行占位。（保养占1，维修占2）","by":"黄浩 Cokey"}$j$::jsonb),
('p170','EAS-2026-PBS-004',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-11","text":"- 调用英国 AI 技师 上线一个月数据，完成9,616条记录的数据深度分析，回复完成率98.7%，命中率80.6%，平均处理时间9.46秒；重点识别出569条未有效回应用户诉求的回复，以及保养\\保修问题命中率仅18.2%、部分回答遗漏重点及重复发送欢迎语等问题，形成专项分析报告及整改建议。\n- 推进 AI 技师在欧洲16个国家上线，已将隐私政策及使用协议提交欧洲法务 Duo 审核，待审核完成后推进推广。\n- 车机 AI 问答知识库正式环境上线，协调开展售后知识管理及问答效果测试","by":"黄浩 Cokey"}$j$::jsonb),
('p170','EAS-2026-PBS-004',1,$j${"date":"2026-10-28","text":"- 自研模型仍处在沟通阶段，暂无进展。问答后台测试环境已上线，拉通客服团队开始进行售后知识导入工作\n\n- 英国AI技师功能已超4000名用户使用，计划12月推广泛欧上线（优先保证五大，波兰市场上线），正在进行法务协议及多市场上线前系统准备及配置工作。","by":"黄浩 Cokey"}$j$::jsonb),
('p172','EAS-2025-UOP-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-11","text":"1. 梦想值英国市场已经完成上线\n2. 德国、法国、西班牙、意大利4大市场的梦想值与本地市场在沟通可提供的权益，目前意大利可提供AC门票，但数量待定。","by":"易鑫 Cassie"}$j$::jsonb),
('p172','EAS-2025-UOP-001',1,$j${"date":"2026-10-28","text":"1、社区预热已经上线\n2、本周内开启梦想值开关\n3、已经下发梦想值在德国、法国、西班牙、意大利上线需求，待产品排期","by":"易鑫 Cassie"}$j$::jsonb),
('p173','EAS-2025-UOP-002',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-11","text":"——取送车券：\n【APP端】权益中心入口页面展示与跳转功能，唐莹反馈1230版本上线\n【BGPC端】需通过BGPC获取零售客户信息，需求单已下发，待产品发起评审方案。\n\n已评审取送车在服务板块的页面跳转与展示等，核销流程待与BSS下午开会评审\n\n——保养券：\n【物料】5大市场翻译版本物料已全部完成，本地社区也已确认。\n【上线】可准备上线5大市场权益中心，目前北欧市场也有发放保养券需求，待本地确认好车主信息后，也可支持配合上线","by":"易鑫 Cassie"}$j$::jsonb),
('p173','EAS-2025-UOP-002',1,$j${"date":"2026-10-28","text":"保养券：\n1、BSS功能已经完成上线\n2、因之前本地市场使用需要根据车型、工时等不同变量配置太多的保养Campaign，因此此次在本地市场宣导前由Janson团队Eric提前做好不同保养类型的配置，比如atto3 为基础做的案例内容，BYD ATTO 3 不同车型年份的保养服务包，采用 Lite Service、Standard Service 和 Pro Service 在系统作为统一命名规则\n\n取送车券：\n【产品端】产品已输出取送车券页面入口&展示方案，支持做跳转功能，具体权益中心界面方案下午拉会与@唐莹沟通确认\n【BGPC端】需通过BGPC获取零售客户信息，已经完成法务评估\n【BSS端】发放取送车券以及核销流程闭环方案已经确认，可拉产品做最终评审进入开发阶段","by":"易鑫 Cassie"}$j$::jsonb),
('p174','EAS-2026-UOP-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-11","text":"财法税：\n1. 已经确认用荷兰荷兰税号覆盖欧陆本地，并以此税号完成相关发票模板\n2. 法务评审风险项已汇报，涉及1130及1230整改的系统问题已经同步，待新技术院评估\n3. 产品合规风险已经与精品部同步拉会，目前精品部负责输出产品相关的物料信息（产品包装，合格证，使用说明，标签等），要求完成节点在11/13\n备货：\n1. 已经完成荷兰备件仓精品备货准备\n商品上线准备：\n1. 已经完成上线所有商品的文案输出，完成1套详情页设计，预计11/18前完成商品详情页多语言版本内容","by":"易鑫 Cassie"}$j$::jsonb),
('p174','EAS-2026-UOP-001',1,$j${"date":"2026-10-28","text":"财法税：\n1、西班牙利润中心已走流程，法国德国意大利确认利润中心组代码\n2、发票模板税务马开丽在10.28日前提供\n采购：\n京东泛欧采购流程已经发起，1130上线在德国、法国部署本地仓储物流。德国覆盖德国、西班牙、意大利运输\n客服：\n1、10月28日完成精品第一场UK产品培训\n2、800电话IVR的按键选择配音增加法德意西，1115前完成测试\n备货：\n1、已经完成法国德国仓库进行小批量空运备货","by":"易鑫 Cassie"}$j$::jsonb),
('p203','EAS-2025-CVS-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-11","text":"本周三前往德国和Carry Group召开现场会议，重点讨论合同商务条款及后续合作方案。","by":"杨琛Chen"}$j$::jsonb),
('p203','EAS-2025-CVS-001',1,$j${"date":"2026-10-28","text":"会议安排： 计划于 11 月与 Carry Group 召开会议，讨论首批订单的采购数量，目前正等待对方确认。\n新增需求： Carry Group 提出新增需求，希望我方提供过去两年的销量数据，作为评估及确定首批订单数量的参考依据。\n后续行动： 整理并提供过去两年的销量数据，跟进 Carry Group 对首批订单数量的确认，并根据双方沟通结果进一步推进项目，尽力争取项目于 12 月底前完成。","by":"杨琛Chen"}$j$::jsonb),
('p204','EAS-2026-CVS-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-11","text":"申请结项","by":"杨琛Chen"}$j$::jsonb),
('p204','EAS-2026-CVS-001',1,$j${"date":"2026-10-28","text":"1. 完成技术研讨会和区域经理大会的介绍分享，重点展示平台实际应用，获得较好反馈。\n2. 持续优化在线平台的UI展示功能，以及新增故障分析及工单处理效率分析功能。","by":"杨琛Chen"}$j$::jsonb),
('p205','EAS-2026-CVS-003',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-11","text":"跟欧洲采购团队进行了深入沟通，目前得到的正式答复：采购不介入。\n欧洲采购团队找了国内汽车事业群的采购经理，得到的反馈是售后服务商目前都是业务部门与服务商直接的商务合作，采购没有介入，所以他们也不介入","by":"杨琛Chen"}$j$::jsonb),
('p205','EAS-2026-CVS-003',1,$j${"date":"2026-10-28","text":"采购一直未给出明确回复，已经把本项目的SOP，以及单独整理的采购流程，发给Viking，等待给出最终的确认","by":"杨琛Chen"}$j$::jsonb),
('p210','EAS-2024-TEC-001',0,$j${"date":"2026-11-11","text":"下次项目会请示关闭","by":"赵栋Alex"}$j$::jsonb),
